      "math_academy_id": "e-21544",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+4{t}^{2}+t-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{t}^{2}+5t+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite the system of linear ODEs in matrix form.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's rewrite our system, highlighting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=(-2)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+(-1)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+4\\cdot {t}^{2}+1\\cdot t+(-2) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+0\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+(-1)\\cdot {t}^{2}+5\\cdot t+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in matrix form:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14219741/assets/911797f16b5767976e8dcf3fc1794b6b69a944c156031b917fdd0b200d5cbb16.svg)\nwhere ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14219741/assets/8b0b144ae73004d067860b6d9f564b3062b4347e57e5a5a32a34e5b750294a1b.svg)",
